edit(f,'This chain explains the division among the six projected-geometry files. \\code{ProjectedCurvature} establishes the parameter-space algebra and calculus; \\code{LocalProjectedCurvature} localizes the hypotheses; \\code{GlobalRangeBundle} constructs the atlas; \\code{GlobalProjectedConnection} defines and glues the connection; \\code{ManifoldProjectedCurvature} proves the actual global curvature formula; \\code{ProjectedBundleCompletion} supplies intrinsic section, gauge and fiber-form compatibility. Treating only the earliest chart file as current coverage would miss the later global constructions.','The six files on projected geometry follow this mathematical development. \\code{ProjectedCurvature} establishes the algebra and calculus on the parameter space. \\code{LocalProjectedCurvature} makes the hypotheses local, and \\code{GlobalRangeBundle} constructs the atlas. \\code{GlobalProjectedConnection} defines the connection and proves that its local descriptions agree. \\code{ManifoldProjectedCurvature} proves the global curvature formula. Finally, \\code{ProjectedBundleCompletion} proves compatibility with intrinsic sections, gauge transformations and the curvature form on each fiber. The later global constructions extend the results of the earliest chart file.')

